      "artist": "leocvlauzon",
      "description": "Molo Plaza in Iloilo is probably one of the best public places in Iloilo. It is located at the very heart of  the town.  The Plaza is very well maintained and full of huge old Balete and Kalachuchi trees. Just this year, the plaza was made open again to the public after it underwent major renovations.  One of the most prominent structures in the plaza are the life-size statues of Roman Goddesses and infamous women warriors.  Beside the plaza is the majestic Molo Church built in 1863.",
